  "worked_solution": "The third equation states that $z=3.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get  \n\n$$\ny+(3)=2\\,⟹\\,y=2-3=-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we substitute $z=3$ and $y=-1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx-(-1)-(3)=4\\,⟹\\,x=4-1+3=6.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=6$, $y=-1$, and $z=3.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as\n$[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$",
